Now let me understand the current state. Both bot.js and captcha_discord.js render the map byte as R=G=B=c (grayscale), which is wrong — they should use the Minecraft map palette. Also they don't handle chunked map data (packet.data may be partial with x/z/width/height... in protocol, the map packet has fields: itemDamage (map id), scale, trackingPosition, locked, icons, columns/width, rows/height, x, z, data). Actually in 1.20.1 the map packet in minecraft-protocol is: `mapId`, `scale`, `trackingPosition`, `locked`, `icons`, `columns` (width), `rows` (height), `x`, `z`, `data`. Hmm, let me recall the protocol spec:

Map packet (0x26 in 1.20.1):
- Map ID: VarInt
- Scale: Byte
- Tracking Position: Boolean
- Locked: Boolean
- Icon Count: VarInt
- Icons...
